          "caption": "Snaefell Summit Reached by the Snaefell Mountain Railway from Laxey.  The Hopkinson bow-collectors used on these cars are unique in the world.  The cars take about half an hour for the journey from Laxey, but with the ex-Aachen motors as fitted in the 1970s, they could, if necessary, do it in under ten minutes.",
