          "path": "_m/g/c/s/u/snaefell-summit-railway-station-wp/29-07-17-snaefell-summit-no-6-.jpg",
          "filename": "29.07.17 Snaefell Summit No.6 (36313916495).jpg",
          "caption": "Snaefell Mountain Railway no.6 at the terminus station on 29 July 2017. Having arrived in on the 14:45 from Laxey, it has a generous 25 minute turnaround time before forming the 15:40 back. Some 2,036 feet (620 metres) above sea level offering views right across the Isle of Man as well as Scotland, England, Wales and Northern Ireland. There is no road access so everything brought in for the café etc. comes by train. \n\nSteps to the trig point marking the actual summit lead from the left hand side of the photo.",
          "alt": "Snaefell Mountain Railway no.6 at the terminus station on 29 July 2017. Having arrived in on the 14:45 from Laxey, it has a generous 25 minute turnaround time before forming the 15:40 back. Some 2,036 feet (620 metres) above sea level offering views right across the Isle of Man as well as Scotland, England, Wales and Northern Ireland. There is no road access so everything brought in for the café etc. comes by train. \n\nSteps to the trig point marking the actual summit lead from the left hand side of the photo.",
          "width": 5180,
          "height": 3899,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Phil Richards from London, UK",
